---
description: Admin mutation authorization
globs: apps/admin/src/lib/*actions.ts,apps/admin/src/app/api/**/route.ts,apps/admin/src/lib/auth-guard.ts
---

- DynamoDB has no row-level security. Every mutating server action and non-auth API route must call `requireAdmin()` from `apps/admin/src/lib/auth-guard.ts`.
- Middleware only checks for a session cookie and is UX/navigation protection, not authorization.
- The Better Auth catch-all (`src/app/api/auth/[...all]/route.ts`) is the only public mutating route.
- `apps/admin/src/lib/authorization-guardrail.test.ts` must fail if a new mutating file omits `requireAdmin()`. Update that inventory when adding a route — do not weaken the assertion.
